# LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the blobs.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true holds CRLF copies of
# LF blobs. The skill lock hashes are computed from the index so they no longer
# care (see tests/scripts/validate-skills.mjs), but everything else in the repo
# still does: `npx skills add <local path>` hashes the files on disk, so the same
# checkout installs with different hashes than CI computes, and the bash test
# harness and hook scripts are read by tools that treat a trailing CR as part of
# the last argument.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content, so assets/logo.png and any
# future binary are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so no filter is attempted regardless of content sniffing.
*.png binary
